/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · Joshua chapters 11-15
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("joshua", [
{n:11, name:"The Northern Campaign", seal:{ref:"Joshua 11:23",verse:"So Joshua took the whole land, according to all that the LORD said unto Moses; and Joshua gave it for an inheritance unto Israel according to their divisions by their tribes. And the land rested from war."},
 facts:["Did you know the battle at the waters of Merom was Israel's largest battle yet? Jabin of Hazor gathered kings from across the north into one vast army.", "Did you know Hazor was the greatest Canaanite city in the north? Its ruins cover about 200 acres, and it alone of the northern cities was burned.", "Did you know the Anakim were the giants who terrified Israel's spies forty years earlier? Joshua cut them off from the hill country, and the land rested from war."],
 questions:[
  {q:"Who was the king of Hazor who rallied the northern kings against Israel?", options:["Jabin","Jobab","Japhia","Debir"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 11:1",verse:"And it came to pass, when Jabin king of Hazor had heard those things, that he sent to Jobab king of Madon, and to the king of Shimron, and to the king of Achshaph,",
   insight:"Jabin of Hazor was the ringleader of the northern alliance, and his city is called the head of all those kingdoms."},
  {q:"Which people lived under Hermon in the land of Mizpeh and joined Jabin's alliance?", options:["The Hivites","The Girgashites","The Kenites","The Kadmonites"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 11:3",verse:"And to the Canaanite on the east and on the west, and to the Amorite, and the Hittite, and the Perizzite, and the Jebusite in the mountains, and to the Hivite under Hermon in the land of Mizpeh.",
   insight:"The alliance drew in peoples from every direction, yet their numbers could not stand against the LORD's promise to Joshua."},
  {q:"How large was the allied army that gathered against Israel?", options:["As the sand that is upon the sea shore in multitude","As the stars of heaven for number","As the locusts covering the land","As the dust of the earth for weight"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 11:4",verse:"And they went out, they and all their hosts with them, much people, even as the sand that is upon the sea shore in multitude, with horses and chariots very many.",
   insight:"An army beyond counting gathered against Israel, but God had already promised Joshua the victory."},
  {q:"Where did the allied kings pitch their camps together to fight against Israel?", options:["At the waters of Merom","At the waters of Meribah","In the valley of Achor","At the brook Besor"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 11:5",verse:"And when all these kings were met together, they came and pitched together at the waters of Merom, to fight against Israel.",
   insight:"The kings massed at Merom in the far north, choosing the ground where they felt strongest, and lost everything there."},
  {q:"What did the LORD tell Joshua to do to the enemy horses?", options:["Hough them","Yoke them to Israel's chariots","Send them back to Egypt","Offer them at the altar"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 11:6",verse:"And the LORD said unto Joshua, Be not afraid because of them: for to morrow about this time will I deliver them up all slain before Israel: thou shalt hough their horses, and burn their chariots with fire.",
   insight:"God told Joshua to cripple the captured horses so Israel would trust in Him, not in stolen warhorses."},
  {q:"What did the LORD command Joshua to do with the enemy chariots?", options:["Burn them with fire","Keep them for Israel's army","Hide them in the hills","Give them to the Gibeonites"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 11:6",verse:"And the LORD said unto Joshua, Be not afraid because of them: for to morrow about this time will I deliver them up all slain before Israel: thou shalt hough their horses, and burn their chariots with fire.",
   insight:"Burning the chariots was a confession that the victory belonged to God, not to military strength."},
  {q:"How did Joshua's attack on the northern alliance begin?", options:["He came against them suddenly","He sent a demand for surrender first","He waited forty days in the hills","He divided his army into seven parts"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 11:7",verse:"So Joshua came, and all the people of war with him, against them by the waters of Merom suddenly; and they fell upon them.",
   insight:"Swift, obedient action caught the great alliance unprepared; Joshua did not delay once God had spoken."},
  {q:"How far did Israel chase the fleeing enemy?", options:["Unto great Zidon and Misrephoth-maim","Unto the river Euphrates","Unto the mountains of Seir","Unto the gates of Damascus"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 11:8",verse:"And the LORD delivered them into the hand of Israel, who smote them, and chased them unto great Zidon, and unto Misrephoth-maim, and unto the valley of Mizpeh eastward; and they smote them, until they left them none remaining.",
   insight:"Israel pursued the enemy to the far coast and the eastern valley; the victory was thorough, not partial."},
  {q:"Which valley eastward did the chase reach?", options:["The valley of Mizpeh","The valley of Jezreel","The valley of Elah","The valley of Berachah"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 11:8",verse:"And the LORD delivered them into the hand of Israel, who smote them, and chased them unto great Zidon, and unto Misrephoth-maim, and unto the valley of Mizpeh eastward; and they smote them, until they left them none remaining.",
   insight:"From the sea coast to the valley of Mizpeh, no part of the enemy army found a place to regroup."},
  {q:"Why did Joshua turn back and take Hazor itself?", options:["Because Hazor beforetime was the head of all those kingdoms","Because its walls were the lowest","Because the Gibeonites asked him to","Because it held Israel's stolen cattle"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 11:10",verse:"And Joshua at that time turned back, and took Hazor, and smote the king thereof with the sword: for Hazor beforetime was the head of all those kingdoms.",
   insight:"Joshua struck at the head of the alliance; when the leading city fell, the northern resistance collapsed."},
  {q:"How did the king of Hazor die?", options:["He was smitten with the sword","He fell from the city wall","He was burned in his palace","He drowned in the waters of Merom"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 11:10",verse:"And Joshua at that time turned back, and took Hazor, and smote the king thereof with the sword: for Hazor beforetime was the head of all those kingdoms.",
   insight:"Jabin, who had gathered the nations against Israel, fell by the sword like the least of his soldiers."},
  {q:"What happened to every soul in Hazor?", options:["They were smitten with the edge of the sword, and none was left to breathe","They were carried captive to Gilgal","They were made servants to Israel","They fled to the cities of refuge"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 11:11",verse:"And they smote all the souls that were therein with the edge of the sword, utterly destroying them: there was not any left to breathe: and he burnt Hazor with fire.",
   insight:"The utter destruction of Hazor was God's judgment on a city steeped in the evils He had long warned about."},
  {q:"Of all the cities that stood still in their strength, which one alone did Joshua burn?", options:["Hazor","Madon","Shimron","Achshaph"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 11:13",verse:"But as for the cities that stood still in their strength, Israel burned none of them, save Hazor only; that did Joshua burn.",
   insight:"Only Hazor was burned, the head city, a sign that God judges the centers of rebellion most severely."},
  {q:"What did the children of Israel do with the spoil of these cities and the cattle?", options:["They took them for a prey unto themselves","They burned them with the cities","They left them for the wild beasts","They gave them to the priests alone"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 11:14",verse:"And all the spoil of these cities, and the cattle, the children of Israel took for a prey unto themselves; but every man they smote with the edge of the sword, until they had destroyed them, neither left they any to breathe.",
   insight:"The spoil was Israel's lawful reward, but every person was devoted to destruction as God had commanded."},
  {q:"How much of what the LORD commanded Moses did Joshua leave undone?", options:["Nothing; he left nothing undone","Only the burning of Hazor","Only the pursuit to Zidon","Only the division of the spoil"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 11:15",verse:"As the LORD commanded Moses his servant, so did Moses command Joshua, and so did Joshua; he left nothing undone of all that the LORD commanded Moses.",
   insight:"Joshua's greatness was simple: he did all that God commanded, leaving nothing undone."},
  {q:"From where to where did Joshua take the land in this campaign?", options:["From mount Halak by Seir to Baal-gad in the valley of Lebanon","From Kadesh-barnea to the river Euphrates","From the Arnon to the Jabbok","From Beersheba to Dan"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 11:17",verse:"Even from the mount Halak, that goeth up to Seir, even unto Baal-gad in the valley of Lebanon under mount Hermon: and all their kings he took, and smote them, and slew them.",
   insight:"The campaign swept from the southern hills to the northern valley, securing the whole promised hill country."},
  {q:"How long did Joshua make war with all those kings?", options:["A long time","Forty days","Seven years","One summer"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 11:18",verse:"Joshua made war a long time with all those kings.",
   insight:"The conquest was not won in a day; Joshua fought on patiently for years until the work was done."},
  {q:"Which city alone made peace with the children of Israel?", options:["Gibeon, of the Hivites","Jericho","Hazor","Lachish"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 11:19",verse:"There was not a city that made peace with the children of Israel, save the Hivites the inhabitants of Gibeon: all other they took in battle.",
   insight:"Gibeon alone sought peace and found it; every city that fought was taken, but mercy was open to any who asked."},
  {q:"Why did the LORD harden the hearts of these kings to meet Israel in battle?", options:["That He might destroy them utterly, as He commanded Moses","That Israel might learn their crafts","That they might serve in the tabernacle","That their horses could be taken alive"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 11:20",verse:"For it was of the LORD to harden their hearts, that they should come against Israel in battle, that he might destroy them utterly, and that they might have no favour, but that he might destroy them, as the LORD commanded Moses.",
   insight:"After generations of mercy, God gave these hardened kingdoms over to the judgment their own choices had earned."},
  {q:"Whom did Joshua cut off from the mountains, from Hebron, Debir, and Anab?", options:["The Anakims","The Rephaim","The Zamzummim","The Emim"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 11:21",verse:"And at that time came Joshua, and cut off the Anakims from the mountains, from Hebron, from Debir, from Anab, and from all the mountains of Judah, and from all the mountains of Israel: Joshua destroyed them utterly with their cities.",
   insight:"The Anakim, the giants who had terrified the spies forty years before, were at last cut off from the hills."}
 ]},
{n:12, name:"The Thirty-One Kings", seal:{ref:"Joshua 12:24",verse:"The king of Tirzah, one: all the kings thirty and one."},
 facts:["Did you know this chapter is a roll of honor? It lists every king defeated on both sides of the Jordan, so no victory would be forgotten.", "Did you know Moses defeated Sihon and Og before Israel ever crossed the Jordan? Their lands east of the river went to Reuben, Gad, and half of Manasseh.", "Did you know the total comes to thirty-one kings? The list runs from Jericho, where the conquest began, to Tirzah in the north."],
 questions:[
  {q:"From where to where did the conquests of Moses stretch east of the Jordan?", options:["From the river Arnon unto mount Hermon","From the Red Sea unto the Euphrates","From Kadesh-barnea unto Gaza","From the Jabbok unto the salt sea"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 12:1",verse:"Now these are the kings of the land, which the children of Israel smote, and possessed their land on the other side Jordan toward the rising of the sun, from the river Arnon unto mount Hermon, and all the plain on the east:",
   insight:"Moses' victories east of the Jordan stretched from the Arnon gorge to the snows of Hermon, a vast territory won before Joshua's day."},
  {q:"Who was Sihon?", options:["King of the Amorites, who dwelt in Heshbon","King of Bashan, of the remnant of the giants","King of the Midianites at Peor","King of Edom at mount Seir"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 12:2",verse:"Sihon king of the Amorites, who dwelt in Heshbon, and ruled from Aroer, which is upon the bank of the river Arnon, and from the middle of the river, and from half Gilead, even unto the river Jabbok, which is the border of the children of Ammon;",
   insight:"Sihon refused Israel passage and lost his kingdom; God gave his land to Israel instead."},
  {q:"Which city was Sihon's royal seat?", options:["Heshbon","Ashtaroth","Edrei","Rabbah"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 12:2",verse:"Sihon king of the Amorites, who dwelt in Heshbon, and ruled from Aroer, which is upon the bank of the river Arnon, and from the middle of the river, and from half Gilead, even unto the river Jabbok, which is the border of the children of Ammon;",
   insight:"Heshbon, Sihon's capital, became a city of Reuben, a reminder that proud thrones do not last."},
  {q:"Og king of Bashan was of the remnant of whom?", options:["The giants","The Horites","The Avim","The Caphtorim"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 12:4",verse:"And the coast of Og king of Bashan, which was of the remnant of the giants, that dwelt at Ashtaroth and at Edrei,",
   insight:"Og was one of the last of the giants, yet his size could not save his kingdom from Israel's God."},
  {q:"In which two cities did Og dwell?", options:["Ashtaroth and Edrei","Heshbon and Dibon","Jazer and Gilead","Salcah and Kenath"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 12:4",verse:"And the coast of Og king of Bashan, which was of the remnant of the giants, that dwelt at Ashtaroth and at Edrei,",
   insight:"Og's twin royal cities, Ashtaroth and Edrei, fell with him, and Bashan became Israel's pastureland."},
  {q:"Which two peoples lived on the borders of Og's kingdom?", options:["The Geshurites and the Maachathites","The Ammonites and the Moabites","The Edomites and the Amalekites","The Perizzites and the Girgashites"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 12:5",verse:"And reigned in mount Hermon, and in Salcah, and in all Bashan, unto the border of the Geshurites and the Maachathites, and half Gilead, the border of Sihon king of Heshbon.",
   insight:"Scripture records even the border peoples of Og's land; nothing in God's record is vague or forgotten."},
  {q:"Who smote Sihon and Og?", options:["Moses the servant of the LORD and the children of Israel","Joshua and the tribe of Judah","Caleb and Othniel","Eleazar and the Levites"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 12:6",verse:"Them did Moses the servant of the LORD and the children of Israel smite: and Moses the servant of the LORD gave it for a possession unto the Reubenites, and the Gadites, and the half tribe of Manasseh.",
   insight:"The chapter honors Moses' victories before honoring Joshua's; God gives each servant his own part in the work."},
  {q:"To which tribes did Moses give the land of Sihon and Og?", options:["The Reubenites, the Gadites, and the half tribe of Manasseh","Judah, Ephraim, and Benjamin","Simeon, Levi, and Issachar","Dan, Naphtali, and Asher"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 12:6",verse:"Them did Moses the servant of the LORD and the children of Israel smite: and Moses the servant of the LORD gave it for a possession unto the Reubenites, and the Gadites, and the half tribe of Manasseh.",
   insight:"The two and a half tribes received their inheritance east of the Jordan, as Moses had promised them."},
  {q:"From where to where did Joshua's conquests run west of the Jordan?", options:["From Baal-gad in the valley of Lebanon unto mount Halak","From Jericho unto Jerusalem","From the sea unto the wilderness","From Gilgal unto Shechem"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 12:7",verse:"And these are the kings of the country which Joshua and the children of Israel smote on this side Jordan on the west, from Baal-gad in the valley of Lebanon even unto the mount Halak, that goeth up to Seir; which Joshua gave unto the tribes of Israel for a possession according to their divisions;",
   insight:"Joshua's conquests matched Moses' in scope, from the northern valley of Lebanon to the southern hills."},
  {q:"Who received the conquered land west of the Jordan?", options:["The tribes of Israel, according to their divisions","The priests and the Levites alone","The Gibeonites who made peace","The Kenites, Moses' kin"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 12:7",verse:"And these are the kings of the country which Joshua and the children of Israel smote on this side Jordan on the west, from Baal-gad in the valley of Lebanon even unto the mount Halak, that goeth up to Seir; which Joshua gave unto the tribes of Israel for a possession according to their divisions;",
   insight:"Joshua gave the land to the tribes by their divisions, keeping the promise God made to Abraham's children."},
  {q:"What six kinds of country did the western conquest include?", options:["Mountains, valleys, plains, springs, wilderness, and south country","Cities, villages, towers, gates, walls, and fields","Rivers, lakes, brooks, fountains, wells, and pools","Forests, vineyards, orchards, gardens, pastures, and deserts"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 12:8",verse:"In the mountains, and in the valleys, and in the plains, and in the springs, and in the wilderness, and in the south country; the Hittites, the Amorites, and the Canaanites, the Perizzites, the Hivites, and the Jebusites:",
   insight:"God's gift covered every kind of land, from mountain springs to desert wilderness; nothing was left out."},
  {q:"Which king heads the list of the kings Joshua defeated?", options:["The king of Jericho","The king of Ai","The king of Jerusalem","The king of Hebron"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 12:9",verse:"The king of Jericho, one; the king of Ai, which is beside Bethel, one;",
   insight:"Jericho heads the list, the first city to fall, where Israel learned that walls fall before God."},
  {q:"Which two kings are named together in the list?", options:["The kings of Jerusalem and Hebron","The kings of Jericho and Ai","The kings of Jarmuth and Lachish","The kings of Eglon and Gezer"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 12:10",verse:"The king of Jerusalem, one; the king of Hebron, one;",
   insight:"Jerusalem and Hebron, two cities of the southern campaign, fell to Joshua's sword and are recorded together."},
  {q:"Which two kings are named together in the list?", options:["The kings of Eglon and Gezer","The kings of Debir and Geder","The kings of Hormah and Arad","The kings of Libnah and Adullam"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 12:12",verse:"The king of Eglon, one; the king of Gezer, one;",
   insight:"Eglon and Gezer, cities of the southern and western campaigns, share a line in the victory roll."},
  {q:"Which two kings are named together in the list?", options:["The kings of Hormah and Arad","The kings of Tappuah and Hepher","The kings of Aphek and Lasharon","The kings of Madon and Hazor"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 12:14",verse:"The king of Hormah, one; the king of Arad, one;",
   insight:"Hormah and Arad, southern cities, were counted among the fallen kings of Canaan."},
  {q:"Which two kings are named together in the list?", options:["The kings of Makkedah and Bethel","The kings of Shimron-meron and Achshaph","The kings of Taanach and Megiddo","The kings of Kedesh and Jokneam"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 12:16",verse:"The king of Makkedah, one; the king of Bethel, one;",
   insight:"Makkedah, where the five kings hid in the cave, and Bethel, the house of God, both yielded their kings."},
  {q:"Which two kings are named together in the list?", options:["The kings of Madon and Hazor","The kings of Dor and Gilgal","The kings of Tirzah and Jericho","The kings of Ai and Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 12:19",verse:"The king of Madon, one; the king of Hazor, one;",
   insight:"Madon and Hazor, leaders of the northern alliance, fell together as their confederacy had risen together."},
  {q:"Which two kings are named together in the list?", options:["The kings of Taanach and Megiddo","The kings of Debir and Geder","The kings of Hormah and Arad","The kings of Libnah and Adullam"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 12:21",verse:"The king of Taanach, one; the king of Megiddo, one;",
   insight:"Taanach and Megiddo guarded the great northern plain, famous in Israel's later battles as well."},
  {q:"Which two kings are named together in the list?", options:["The king of Kedesh and the king of Jokneam of Carmel","The king of Dor and the king of Gilgal","The king of Tirzah and the king of Jericho","The king of Ai and the king of Bethel"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 12:22",verse:"The king of Kedesh, one; the king of Jokneam of Carmel, one;",
   insight:"Kedesh and Jokneam of Carmel, northern strongholds, closed out the list of conquered kings."},
  {q:"How many kings were defeated in all, on both sides of the Jordan?", options:["Thirty and one","Twelve","Forty","Seventy"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 12:24",verse:"The king of Tirzah, one: all the kings thirty and one.",
   insight:"Thirty-one kings, every enemy named and none forgotten, a full account of what God did for Israel."}
 ]},
{n:13, name:"The Land East of Jordan", seal:{ref:"Joshua 13:33",verse:"But unto the tribe of Levi Moses gave not any inheritance: the LORD God of Israel was their inheritance, as he said unto them."},
 facts:["Did you know Joshua was old when this chapter opens, yet the LORD said very much land remained to be possessed? God's people always have work left to do.", "Did you know the Philistines had five great cities, Gaza, Ashdod, Ashkelon, Gath, and Ekron? Goliath himself would one day come from Gath.", "Did you know Levi received no land? Their inheritance was the LORD God of Israel Himself, the greatest portion of all."],
 questions:[
  {q:"How is Joshua described when this chapter opens?", options:["Old and stricken in years","Young and full of vigor","Sick and near to death","Blind and unable to lead"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 13:1",verse:"Now Joshua was old and stricken in years; and the LORD said unto him, Thou art old and stricken in years, and there remaineth yet very much land to be possessed.",
   insight:"Age had not retired Joshua; God still had assignments for His old servant."},
  {q:"What did the LORD say still remained for Joshua?", options:["Very much land to be possessed","A few small villages only","Nothing but rest","One last battle at Ai"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 13:1",verse:"Now Joshua was old and stricken in years; and the LORD said unto him, Thou art old and stricken in years, and there remaineth yet very much land to be possessed.",
   insight:"Even after sweeping victories, much land remained; God's work is larger than any one lifetime."},
  {q:"Which two peoples' lands are named as still remaining?", options:["The Philistines and the Geshurites","The Moabites and the Ammonites","The Edomites and the Amalekites","The Syrians and the Hittites"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 13:2",verse:"This is the land that yet remaineth: all the borders of the Philistines, and all Geshuri,",
   insight:"The coastal Philistines and the northern Geshurites remained unconquered, and both would trouble Israel later."},
  {q:"How many lords ruled the Philistines?", options:["Five","Seven","Three","Twelve"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 13:3",verse:"From Sihor, which is before Egypt, even unto the borders of Ekron northward, which is counted to the Canaanite: five lords of the Philistines; the Gazathites, and the Ashdothites, the Eshkalonites, the Gittites, and the Ekronites; also the Avites:",
   insight:"The five Philistine lords ruled as a league, a united front Israel would face for generations."},
  {q:"Which city was one of the five Philistine lordships?", options:["Gath","Mizpeh","Joppa","Beersheba"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 13:3",verse:"From Sihor, which is before Egypt, even unto the borders of Ekron northward, which is counted to the Canaanite: five lords of the Philistines; the Gazathites, and the Ashdothites, the Eshkalonites, the Gittites, and the Ekronites; also the Avites:",
   insight:"Gath, one of the five cities, would one day produce Goliath, the giant David faced."},
  {q:"What place marked the far northern limit of the land yet to be taken?", options:["The entering in of Hamath","The river Euphrates","The mountains of Ararat","The sea of Chinnereth"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 13:5",verse:"And the land of the Giblites, and all Lebanon, toward the sunrising, from Baal-gad under mount Hermon unto the entering into Hamath.",
   insight:"God's promised borders reached to the entering of Hamath, far beyond what Israel had yet possessed."},
  {q:"Who promised to drive out the inhabitants of the hill country?", options:["The LORD Himself: them will I drive out","Joshua with his captains","Caleb with the men of Judah","Eleazar with the Levites"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 13:6",verse:"All the inhabitants of the hill country from Lebanon unto Misrephoth-maim, and all the Sidonians, them will I drive out from before the children of Israel: only divide thou it by lot unto the Israelites for an inheritance, as I have commanded thee.",
   insight:"Where Joshua's strength would end, God's would continue; He promised to finish what Israel could not."},
  {q:"How was the remaining land to be divided among the nine and a half tribes?", options:["By lot","By the size of each tribe's army","By Joshua's personal choice","By drawing boundary stones"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 13:7",verse:"Now therefore divide this land for an inheritance unto the nine tribes, and the half tribe of Manasseh,",
   insight:"The lot took the division out of human hands and placed it in God's, where no tribe could complain of favoritism."},
  {q:"Which tribes had already received their inheritance east of the Jordan?", options:["The Reubenites, the Gadites, and the half tribe of Manasseh","Judah and Simeon","Ephraim and Benjamin","Dan and Naphtali"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 13:8",verse:"With whom the Reubenites and the Gadites have received their inheritance, which Moses gave them, beyond Jordan eastward, even as Moses the servant of the LORD gave them;",
   insight:"The two and a half tribes had chosen the east bank, and Moses had sealed their choice before his death."},
  {q:"Where did the eastern territory begin in the south?", options:["From Aroer, upon the bank of the river Arnon","From the plains of Moab by Jericho","From the wilderness of Zin","From the brook of Egypt"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 13:9",verse:"From Aroer, that is upon the bank of the river Arnon, and the city that is in the midst of the river, and all the plain of Medeba unto Dibon;",
   insight:"The Arnon gorge, where Israel first defeated Sihon, became the southern boundary of Reuben's land."},
  {q:"Whose cities, once ruled from Heshbon, were given to Reuben?", options:["Sihon king of the Amorites","Og king of Bashan","Balaam the soothsayer","Eglon king of Moab"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 13:10",verse:"And all the cities of Sihon king of the Amorites, which reigned in Heshbon, unto the border of the children of Ammon;",
   insight:"Sihon's kingdom, won before Israel crossed the Jordan, became Reuben's settled home."},
  {q:"Which two peoples were not expelled and still dwell among Israel?", options:["The Geshurites and the Maachathites","The Hivites and the Jebusites","The Kenites and the Rechabites","The Avim and the Caphtorim"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 13:13",verse:"Nevertheless the children of Israel expelled not the Geshurites, nor the Maachathites: but the Geshurites and the Maachathites dwell among the Israelites until this day.",
   insight:"Unfinished obedience left the Geshurites and Maachathites in the land, a small compromise with lasting consequences."},
  {q:"What inheritance did Moses give to the tribe of Levi?", options:["None; the sacrifices of the LORD God of Israel are their inheritance","The cities of refuge only","A double portion of the spoil","The tithes of the harvests"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 13:14",verse:"Only unto the tribe of Levi he gave none inheritance; the sacrifices of the LORD God of Israel made by fire are their inheritance, as he said unto them.",
   insight:"Levi received no fields because God gave them something better: Himself, served at His altar."},
  {q:"Which of these was one of Reuben's cities in the plain?", options:["Dibon","Jericho","Bethel","Lachish"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 13:16",verse:"And their coast was from Aroer, that is on the bank of the river Arnon, and the city that is in the midst of the river, and all the plain by Medeba;",
   insight:"Dibon and the plain cities show how fully God settled Reuben in Sihon's former kingdom."},
  {q:"How many princes of Sihon, dukes dwelling in the country, were slain?", options:["Five: Evi, Rekem, Zur, Hur, and Reba","Seven","Three","Twelve"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 13:21",verse:"And all the cities of the plain, and all the kingdom of Sihon king of the Amorites, which reigned in Heshbon, whom Moses smote with the princes of Midian, Evi, and Rekem, and Zur, and Hur, and Reba, which were dukes of Sihon, dwelling in the country.",
   insight:"Even Sihon's vassal princes are named among the slain; no ally of rebellion escaped the record."},
  {q:"What was Balaam the son of Beor called, and how did he die?", options:["The soothsayer, slain with the sword","The prophet, stoned at Peor","The priest, burned at Tophet","The diviner, drowned in Jordan"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 13:22",verse:"Balaam also the son of Beor, the soothsayer, did the children of Israel slay with the sword among them that were slain by them.",
   insight:"Balaam, who tried to curse Israel for Balak's wages, died by the sword among Israel's enemies."},
  {q:"What formed the border of the children of Reuben?", options:["Jordan and its border","The river Arnon","The mountains of Gilead","The wilderness of Kedemoth"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 13:23",verse:"And the border of the children of Reuben was Jordan, and the border thereof. This was the inheritance of the children of Reuben after their families, the cities and the villages thereof.",
   insight:"The Jordan itself bounded Reuben's land, the river that had parted for Israel now marking their home."},
  {q:"Which city marked Gad's territory in Gilead?", options:["Jazer","Ramoth","Mahanaim","Penuel"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 13:25",verse:"And their coast was Jazer, and all the cities of Gilead, and half the land of the children of Ammon, unto Aroer that is before Rabbah;",
   insight:"Jazer and the cities of Gilead gave Gad rich pastureland, fitting for a tribe rich in cattle."},
  {q:"To whom did Moses give half of Gilead, Ashtaroth, and Edrei?", options:["The children of Machir the son of Manasseh","The children of Jair","The sons of Hezron","The daughters of Zelophehad"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 13:31",verse:"And half Gilead, and Ashtaroth, and Edrei, cities of the kingdom of Og in Bashan, were pertaining unto the children of Machir the son of Manasseh, even to the one half of the children of Machir by their families.",
   insight:"Machir, Manasseh's warrior son, received Og's former royal cities as his family's portion."},
  {q:"What was the inheritance of the Levites?", options:["The LORD God of Israel was their inheritance","The cities of refuge and their suburbs","The firstfruits of every harvest","The spoil of every battle"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 13:33",verse:"But unto the tribe of Levi Moses gave not any inheritance: the LORD God of Israel was their inheritance, as he said unto them.",
   insight:"The Levites' portion was not land but the LORD Himself, the greatest inheritance any tribe could hold."}
 ]},
{n:14, name:"Caleb Claims Hebron", seal:{ref:"Joshua 14:14",verse:"Hebron therefore became the inheritance of Caleb the son of Jephunneh the Kenezite unto this day, because that he wholly followed the LORD God of Israel."},
 facts:["Did you know Caleb waited forty-five years for this moment? Moses swore the promise when Caleb was forty, and he claimed it at eighty-five.", "Did you know Caleb asked for the hardest ground in Judah? The mountain of Hebron was held by the Anakim, the very giants who had terrified Israel.", "Did you know Hebron was once called Kirjath-arba? It was named for Arba, a great man among the Anakim, before Caleb took it."],
 questions:[
  {q:"Who divided the land west of the Jordan among the tribes?", options:["Eleazar the priest, Joshua, and the heads of the fathers","Moses and Aaron","The twelve spies","The elders of each city"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 14:1",verse:"And these are the countries which the children of Israel inherited in the land of Canaan, which Eleazar the priest, and Joshua the son of Nun, and the heads of the fathers of the tribes of the children of Israel, distributed for inheritance to them.",
   insight:"Priest, leader, and tribal heads divided the land together; great work in Israel was never one man's alone."},
  {q:"By what means was the inheritance divided?", options:["By lot, as the LORD commanded by the hand of Moses","By measuring each tribe's fighting men","By the order the tribes crossed Jordan","By casting stones into the ark"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 14:2",verse:"By lot was their inheritance, as the LORD commanded by the hand of Moses, for the nine tribes, and for the half tribe.",
   insight:"The lot placed every tribe's portion in God's hands, beyond quarreling or favor."},
  {q:"How many tribes had Moses already settled east of the Jordan?", options:["Two and a half","Three and a half","One and a half","Four"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 14:3",verse:"For Moses had given the inheritance of two tribes and an half tribe on the other side Jordan: but unto the Levites he gave none inheritance among them.",
   insight:"Reuben, Gad, and half of Manasseh were already settled, so the lot covered only the nine and a half tribes west of Jordan."},
  {q:"Why did the Levites receive no portion of the land?", options:["The children of Joseph were two tribes, and the Levites were given cities to dwell in","They had forfeited it at Kadesh-barnea","They chose the priesthood instead","They arrived too late for the lot"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 14:4",verse:"For the children of Joseph were two tribes, Manasseh and Ephraim: therefore they gave no part unto the Levites in the land, save cities to dwell in, with their suburbs for their cattle and for their substance.",
   insight:"Joseph's double portion through Ephraim and Manasseh kept the tribes at twelve, while Levi served God in cities scattered through them all."},
  {q:"What did the children of Israel do about the division?", options:["As the LORD commanded Moses, so they did","They argued for better portions","They asked for the division to wait","They gave the best land to Judah first"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 14:5",verse:"As the LORD commanded Moses, so the children of Israel did, and they divided the land.",
   insight:"Simple obedience marked the division; they did as the LORD commanded, and the land was peacefully shared."},
  {q:"Who came to Joshua in Gilgal with the children of Judah?", options:["Caleb the son of Jephunneh the Kenezite","Othniel the son of Kenaz","Eleazar the priest","The elders of Hebron"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 14:6",verse:"Then the children of Judah came unto Joshua in Gilgal: and Caleb the son of Jephunneh the Kenezite said unto him, Thou knowest the thing that the LORD said unto Moses the man of God concerning me and thee in Kadesh-barnea.",
   insight:"Caleb came with Judah's blessing to claim the promise Moses had sworn to him forty-five years before."},
  {q:"How old was Caleb when Moses sent him to spy out the land from Kadesh-barnea?", options:["Forty years old","Thirty years old","Fifty years old","Sixty years old"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 14:7",verse:"Forty years old was I when Moses the servant of the LORD sent me from Kadesh-barnea to espy out the land; and I brought him word again as it was in mine heart.",
   insight:"At forty Caleb had stood against the fearful majority; at eighty-five he would finish what he started."},
  {q:"What set Caleb apart from his brethren who went up with him?", options:["He wholly followed the LORD his God","He was the strongest of the spies","He was the eldest of the twelve","He brought back the largest cluster of grapes"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 14:8",verse:"Nevertheless my brethren that went up with me made the heart of the people melt: but I wholly followed the LORD my God.",
   insight:"Wholehearted following was Caleb's distinction; he did not follow God halfway or with reservations."},
  {q:"What did Moses swear to Caleb?", options:["The land whereon thy feet have trodden shall be thine inheritance","Thou shalt lead Israel after Joshua","Thy sons shall be priests forever","Thou shalt see the land but not enter it"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 14:9",verse:"And Moses sware on that day, saying, Surely the land whereon thy feet have trodden shall be thine inheritance, and thy children’s for ever, because thou hast wholly followed the LORD my God.",
   insight:"God remembered the oath sworn to Caleb through forty-five wilderness years, and now the day of payment had come."},
  {q:"How many years had passed since Kadesh-barnea, and how old was Caleb now?", options:["Forty-five years; eighty-five years old","Forty years; eighty years old","Thirty-eight years; seventy-eight years","Fifty years; ninety years old"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 14:10",verse:"And now, behold, the LORD hath kept me alive, as he said, these forty and five years, even since the LORD spake this word unto Moses, while the children of Israel wandered in the wilderness: and now, lo, I am this day fourscore and five years old.",
   insight:"Forty-five years of waiting had not dimmed Caleb's faith; he claimed the promise as boldly as he first believed it."},
  {q:"How strong was Caleb at eighty-five?", options:["As strong as he was the day Moses sent him","Weaker, but wise in counsel","Strong enough to advise, not to fight","Strong in spirit, feeble in body"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 14:11",verse:"As yet I am as strong this day as I was in the day that Moses sent me: as my strength was then, even so is my strength now, for war, both to go out, and to come in.",
   insight:"God renewed Caleb's strength for the battle ahead; faith kept him young enough for giants."},
  {q:"What did Caleb ask Joshua to give him?", options:["This mountain, where the Anakim dwell","The city of Gilgal","The valley of Achor","The plains of Jericho"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 14:12",verse:"Now therefore give me this mountain, whereof the LORD spake in that day; for thou heardest in that day how the Anakims were there, and that the cities were great and fenced: if so be the LORD will be with me, then I shall be able to drive them out, as the LORD said.",
   insight:"At eighty-five Caleb asked for the hardest ground in the land, the mountain of the giants."},
  {q:"Who lived in the mountain Caleb requested?", options:["The Anakims, in great fenced cities","The Jebusites, in strong towers","The Amorites, in iron chariots","The Philistines, in walled towns"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 14:12",verse:"Now therefore give me this mountain, whereof the LORD spake in that day; for thou heardest in that day how the Anakims were there, and that the cities were great and fenced: if so be the LORD will be with me, then I shall be able to drive them out, as the LORD said.",
   insight:"The Anakim, the giants who had melted Israel's courage, were exactly the foes Caleb wanted to face."},
  {q:"What did Joshua do for Caleb?", options:["He blessed him and gave him Hebron","He made him judge over Judah","He gave him a double portion","He sent him to spy again"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 14:13",verse:"And Joshua blessed him, and gave unto Caleb the son of Jephunneh Hebron for an inheritance.",
   insight:"Joshua, Caleb's fellow faithful spy, gladly blessed him and granted his request."},
  {q:"Why did Hebron become Caleb's inheritance?", options:["Because he wholly followed the LORD God of Israel","Because he was the oldest spy living","Because Judah voted him the land","Because he paid silver for it"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 14:14",verse:"Hebron therefore became the inheritance of Caleb the son of Jephunneh the Kenezite unto this day, because that he wholly followed the LORD God of Israel.",
   insight:"Scripture gives one reason for Caleb's reward: he wholly followed the LORD his God."},
  {q:"What was Hebron called before, and after whom was it named?", options:["Kirjath-arba, after Arba, a great man among the Anakims","Kirjath-sepher, after Sepher the scribe","Kirjath-jearim, after Jearim the woodman","Kirjath-huzoth, after Huzoth the strong"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 14:15",verse:"And the name of Hebron before was Kirjath-arba; which Arba was a great man among the Anakims. And the land had rest from war.",
   insight:"Hebron bore a giant's name until a man of faith took it; the old name gave way to the new owner."},
  {q:"What followed Caleb's victory?", options:["The land had rest from war","Israel crowned a king","The tabernacle was built at Shiloh","The Jubilee was proclaimed"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 14:15",verse:"And the name of Hebron before was Kirjath-arba; which Arba was a great man among the Anakims. And the land had rest from war.",
   insight:"One faithful man's victory helped bring rest to the whole land; faithfulness blesses more than the faithful."},
  {q:"Of what people was Caleb's family?", options:["The Kenezites","The Hivites","The Jebusites","The Perizzites"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 14:6",verse:"Then the children of Judah came unto Joshua in Gilgal: and Caleb the son of Jephunneh the Kenezite said unto him, Thou knowest the thing that the LORD said unto Moses the man of God concerning me and thee in Kadesh-barnea.",
   insight:"Caleb was a Kenezite by birth, yet wholly Israel's by faith; it is following God, not bloodline, that makes a man His."},
  {q:"What kept Caleb alive through the forty-five wilderness years?", options:["The LORD kept him alive, as He had promised","He hid in the caves of Engedi","He lived apart with the Kenites","He stayed behind at Kadesh"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 14:10",verse:"And now, behold, the LORD hath kept me alive, as he said, these forty and five years, even since the LORD spake this word unto Moses, while the children of Israel wandered in the wilderness: and now, lo, I am this day fourscore and five years old.",
   insight:"God's promise preserved Caleb through the wilderness; the LORD keeps alive those He has appointed for His purpose."},
  {q:"By whose hand had the LORD commanded the division of the land?", options:["By the hand of Moses","By the hand of Aaron","By the hand of Eleazar","By the hand of the elders"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 14:2",verse:"By lot was their inheritance, as the LORD commanded by the hand of Moses, for the nine tribes, and for the half tribe.",
   insight:"The lot carried Moses' God-given authority, so every tribe received its portion as from the LORD Himself."}
 ]},
{n:15, name:"Judah's Inheritance", seal:{ref:"Joshua 15:63",verse:"As for the Jebusites the inhabitants of Jerusalem, the children of Judah could not drive them out: but the Jebusites dwell with the children of Judah at Jerusalem unto this day."},
 facts:["Did you know Judah received the largest allotment of any tribe? The chapter names over a hundred of its cities, from the wilderness to the sea.", "Did you know Achsah was one of the boldest women in Scripture? She asked her father Caleb for springs of water, and he gave her the upper and the nether springs.", "Did you know Kirjath-jearim lay within Judah's borders? The ark of God would rest there for twenty years before David brought it to Jerusalem."],
 questions:[
  {q:"Which tribe's lot is described first, and largest, in this chapter?", options:["The tribe of the children of Judah","The tribe of Ephraim","The tribe of Benjamin","The tribe of Dan"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 15:1",verse:"This then was the lot of the tribe of the children of Judah by their families; even to the border of Edom the wilderness of Zin southward was the uttermost part of the south coast.",
   insight:"Judah's lot comes first, the tribe from which the promised King would one day arise."},
  {q:"Where did Judah's south border begin?", options:["At the shore of the salt sea, from the bay that looketh southward","At the river of Egypt","At Kadesh-barnea","At the wilderness of Zin"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 15:2",verse:"And their south border was from the shore of the salt sea, from the bay that looketh southward:",
   insight:"Judah's border began at the Dead Sea's southern bay, a precise landmark no surveyor could dispute."},
  {q:"Which well-known place lay on Judah's south border?", options:["Kadesh-barnea","Mount Sinai","Beersheba","Gerar"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 15:3",verse:"And it went out to the south side to Maaleh-acrabbim, and passed along to Zin, and ascended up on the south side unto Kadesh-barnea, and passed along to Hezron, and went up to Adar, and fetched a compass to Karkaa:",
   insight:"The border passed Kadesh-barnea, where Israel had once refused to enter; now Judah possessed it."},
  {q:"At what river did the south border end at the sea?", options:["The river of Egypt","The river Arnon","The river Jabbok","The river Kishon"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 15:4",verse:"From thence it passed toward Azmon, and went out unto the river of Egypt; and the goings out of that coast were at the sea: this shall be your south coast.",
   insight:"From the Dead Sea to the river of Egypt, Judah's southern line was drawn by God's own measuring."},
  {q:"What formed Judah's east border?", options:["The salt sea, even unto the end of Jordan","The mountains of Moab","The wilderness of Judah","The brook of Egypt"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 15:5",verse:"And the east border was the salt sea, even unto the end of Jordan. And their border in the north quarter was from the bay of the sea at the uttermost part of Jordan:",
   insight:"The salt sea and the Jordan bounded Judah on the east, waters that had witnessed God's mighty acts."},
  {q:"Whose stone marked Judah's north border as it went up?", options:["Bohan the son of Reuben","Jacob the son of Isaac","Gilead the son of Machir","Hezron the son of Perez"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 15:6",verse:"And the border went up to Beth-hogla, and passed along by the north of Beth-arabah; and the border went up to the stone of Bohan the son of Reuben:",
   insight:"Even a man's memorial stone became a national landmark; God weaves ordinary lives into His people's story."},
  {q:"From which valley did the border go up to Debir?", options:["The valley of Achor","The valley of Elah","The valley of Rephaim","The valley of Zeboim"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 15:7",verse:"And the border went up toward Debir from the valley of Achor, and so northward, looking toward Gilgal, that is before the going up to Adummim, which is on the south side of the river: and the border passed toward the waters of En-shemesh, and the goings out thereof were at En-rogel:",
   insight:"The valley of Achor, where Achan's sin was judged, now lay safely inside Judah's inheritance."},
  {q:"Which valley on the north border would later become infamous in Israel's history?", options:["The valley of the son of Hinnom","The valley of Jehoshaphat","The valley of Shaveh","The valley of Succoth"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 15:8",verse:"And the border went up by the valley of the son of Hinnom unto the south side of the Jebusite; the same is Jerusalem: and the border went up to the top of the mountain that lieth before the valley of Hinnom westward, which is at the end of the valley of the giants northward:",
   insight:"The valley of Hinnom would later witness Israel's idolatry; possessing the land was easier than keeping it holy."},
  {q:"What was Baalah also called?", options:["Kirjath-jearim","Kirjath-sepher","Kirjath-arba","Kirjath-huzoth"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 15:9",verse:"And the border was drawn from the top of the hill unto the fountain of the water of Nephtoah, and went out to the cities of mount Ephron; and the border was drawn to Baalah, which is Kirjath-jearim:",
   insight:"Kirjath-jearim would one day shelter the ark of God for twenty years, a quiet town with a holy calling."},
  {q:"Which city did the border reach after passing mount Jearim?", options:["Beth-shemesh","Timnah","Ekron","Libnah"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 15:10",verse:"And the border compassed from Baalah westward unto mount Seir, and passed along unto the side of mount Jearim, which is Chesalon, on the north side, and went down to Beth-shemesh, and passed on to Timnah:",
   insight:"Beth-shemesh, the house of the sun, marked Judah's northwest turn toward the coastal plain."},
  {q:"What formed Judah's west border?", options:["The great sea","The river of Egypt","The mountains of Seir","The valley of Sorek"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 15:12",verse:"And the west border was to the great sea, and the coast thereof. This is the coast of the children of Judah round about according to their families.",
   insight:"The Mediterranean, the great sea, washed Judah's western edge, opening the tribe to the nations beyond."},
  {q:"What portion did Joshua give to Caleb within Judah's lot?", options:["The city of Arba the father of Anak, which is Hebron","The city of Debir with its villages","The valley of Eshcol","The hill country of Ziph"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 15:13",verse:"And unto Caleb the son of Jephunneh he gave a part among the children of Judah, according to the commandment of the LORD to Joshua, even the city of Arba the father of Anak, which city is Hebron.",
   insight:"Caleb's promised mountain lay inside Judah's borders; God's promises to individuals fit within His promises to the people."},
  {q:"Whom did Caleb drive from Hebron?", options:["The three sons of Anak: Sheshai, Ahiman, and Talmai","The five kings of the Amorites","The seven sons of Gibeon","The Jebusites of Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 15:14",verse:"And Caleb drove thence the three sons of Anak, Sheshai, and Ahiman, and Talmai, the children of Anak.",
   insight:"The three sons of Anak are named because real giants fell before a real man's faith."},
  {q:"What was Debir called before?", options:["Kirjath-sepher","Kirjath-arba","Kirjath-jearim","Kirjath-huzoth"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 15:15",verse:"And he went up thence to the inhabitants of Debir: and the name of Debir before was Kirjath-sepher.",
   insight:"Debir, the city of the book, bore an older name; Canaan's cities carried histories long before Israel came."},
  {q:"What did Caleb promise to whoever captured Kirjath-sepher?", options:["Achsah his daughter to wife","Half his inheritance in Hebron","A thousand shekels of silver","The governorship of Debir"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 15:16",verse:"And Caleb said, He that smiteth Kirjath-sepher, and taketh it, to him will I give Achsah my daughter to wife.",
   insight:"Caleb set a warrior's prize for the city's capture, and his own kinsman won it."},
  {q:"Who captured Kirjath-sepher and won Achsah?", options:["Othniel the son of Kenaz, Caleb's brother","Ehud the son of Gera","Shamgar the son of Anath","Jair the Gileadite"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 15:17",verse:"And Othniel the son of Kenaz, the brother of Caleb, took it: and he gave him Achsah his daughter to wife.",
   insight:"Othniel proved his valor at Debir, and God would later raise him as Israel's first judge."},
  {q:"What did Achsah urge Othniel to ask her father for?", options:["A field","A walled city","A thousand cattle","An armed guard"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 15:18",verse:"And it came to pass, as she came unto him, that she moved him to ask of her father a field: and she lighted off her ass; and Caleb said unto her, What wouldest thou?",
   insight:"Achsah had the foresight to secure land for her new household, thinking ahead like a wise builder."},
  {q:"What blessing did Achsah ask of her father?", options:["Springs of water, and he gave her the upper and the nether springs","Vineyards on the hills of Hebron","Flocks to fill the valley","Servants for her household"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 15:19",verse:"Who answered, Give me a blessing; for thou hast given me a south land; give me also springs of water. And he gave her the upper springs, and the nether springs.",
   insight:"Achsah asked boldly for what her land needed most, water, and her father gave her double: the upper and the nether springs."},
  {q:"Which two cities are named together among Judah's valley cities?", options:["Lachish and Eglon","Libnah and Adullam","Jarmuth and Socoh","Keilah and Achzib"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 15:39",verse:"Lachish, and Bozkath, and Eglon,",
   insight:"Lachish and Eglon, taken in Joshua's southern campaign, were now settled cities of Judah's lowland."},
  {q:"What is said of the Jebusites at the chapter's end?", options:["The children of Judah could not drive them out, and they dwell with Judah at Jerusalem unto this day","They made peace and served Judah","They fled to the Philistines","They were utterly destroyed by Caleb"], a:0, ref:"Joshua 15:63",verse:"As for the Jebusites the inhabitants of Jerusalem, the children of Judah could not drive them out: but the Jebusites dwell with the children of Judah at Jerusalem unto this day.",
   insight:"Jerusalem's Jebusites remained, a thorn in Judah's side until David's day; unfinished conquest always leaves a remainder."}
 ]}
]);
